# User Stories

> Master user stories, grouped by feature. **Additive-only** — see `constitution/conventions.md`. Never edit or delete an existing `##` feature section or story from here; only append (via `.wayforge/scripts/merge_master_doc.py`). A feature's own stories live at `features/<slug>/user-stories.md` until merged.

Each feature is its own `##` section:

```
## <feature-slug>

- As a <role>, I want to <action>, so that <benefit>.
  **Acceptance criteria:**
  - [ ] <criterion>
  - [ ] <criterion>
```

- Acceptance criteria here are the same ones `/wayforge-plan` turns into task-level acceptance criteria in `implementation-plan.md`, and that `/wayforge-review` checks off in `review.md` — keep the wording consistent across all three so a reviewer (human or Codex) can trace a criterion back to the story that motivated it.

